book></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NHK SPRING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGINO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HEMMI YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA YOSHIHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGINO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HEMMI, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAMURA, YOSHIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGINO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A simplified tightening device capable of reducing a bolt inserting force and also providing a high tightening force, comprising a base (1) in which a conical hole with slanted surface is formed, a thread block (2) through which a female screw (2b) to be threaded with a bolt (4) is passed and which is guided by the conical hole and expanded or contracted according to the axial movement of the bolt (4) inserted into the base (1), a spring (3) pressing the thread block (2) against the conical hole, and a cap (9) which is provided with a bolt inserting hole (9a), installed on the base (1), and presses the spring (3), wherein the inclination angle of the lower side slanted surfaces (21) of the threads (20) of the female thread (2b) on the thread block (2) is made larger than the inclination angle of the upper side slanted surface (22).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de serrage simplifié capable de réduire la force d'insertion de boulons et également de procurer une force de serrage élevée, comprenant une base (1) dans laquelle est formée un trou conique présentant une surface oblique, un bloc fileté (2) à travers lequel une vis femelle (2b) à visser avec un boulon (4) est passée et laquelle est guidée par le trou conique et sortie ou rentrée selon le mouvement axial du boulon (4) inséré dans la base (1), un ressort (3) exerçant une pression sur le bloc fileté (2) contre le trou conique, ainsi qu'un couvercle (9) lequel est doté d'un trou (9a) d'insertion de boulons, disposé sur la base (1), et appuie contre le ressort (3), l'angle d'inclinaison des surfaces obliques latérales inférieures (21) des filets (20) du filetage femelle (2b) sur le bloc fileté (2) étant supérieur à l'angle d'inclinaison de la surface oblique supérieure latérale (22).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>